mud-builder-client is the browser UI of the MUD Builder (Vite + React 19, dev port 60080, /api proxied to mud-builder-server on 61000). Its design tenets, fixed by the Phase-1 plan: the form editor is the PRIMARY surface; every path to disk goes through an explicit Preview of the exact generated .are text (plus server diff); Download is always available (generated locally via the isomorphic merc-area emitter); raw-text "Manual edit" is allowed but visibly flagged and validated by the parser before it touches the model; and all write actions (Save, Hot reload, Copyover-with-confirm) render disabled with an explanatory tooltip whenever the server reports writes are gated off (/api/capabilities). Phase 1 shipped the rooms slice; Phase 2 shipped the Scripts tab (mob scripts authored against the #SCRIPTS area section, validated live in the browser with the same validateScripts rules the server and the C engine enforce — invalid scripts block Preview/Save before any network call). Phase 3 shipped the Mobs and Objects tabs (full stat forms; object values re-typed per item type via merc-area's objValueKinds; verbatim word fields and unlisted flag bits always preserved) on a shared workbench hook (features/areas/workbench.tsx), plus the deployed build.shatteredarchive.dev containers in the experimental compose stack — the only environment where the server reports writes enabled.
